INT. SKI GONDOLA CABIN - DUSK

Stopped dead mid-cable. Wind knocks the glass. Four seats, four strangers, one dying lamp.

KAVEH ZANDI, 30s, parka, nervous hands, sits facing the door.

LINNEA STRAND, 40s, ski patrol jacket, radio at her hip, stands braced against the wall.

OSWIN PELL, 60s, tweed under his shell, a briefcase chained to his wrist.

JUNO MARCHETTI, 20s, snowboard across her knees, earbuds around her neck.

The cabin lurches. Everyone grabs something.

JUNO
That's not supposed to happen.

LINNEA
It's wind. Stay seated.

Kaveh stares at the briefcase.

KAVEH
What's in the case?

OSWIN
Paperwork.

KAVEH
Chained paperwork.

OSWIN
Very important paperwork.

Linnea thumbs her radio. Static. Nothing.

LINNEA
Base, this is Strand. Base?

Static.

JUNO
Phones?

Kaveh, Juno, Oswin check phones. Three heads shake.

JUNO (CONT'D)
No bars. At all.

KAVEH
Someone cut the tower.

LINNEA
Don't be dramatic.

KAVEH
Nobody jams a tower by accident, Linnea.

LINNEA
You don't know my name.

KAVEH
It's on your jacket.

Beat. Linnea glances down. Her own name patch. She exhales.

The cabin sways. Oswin grips the chain.

OSWIN
I was told this would be a quiet trip.

JUNO
Told by who?

Oswin says nothing.

KAVEH
Open it.

OSWIN
Absolutely not.

KAVEH
Open it or I do.

Kaveh stands. The cabin tilts. Linnea steps between them.

LINNEA
Sit. Down.

Kaveh lunges for the case. Oswin swings it. It cracks Kaveh's chin. Kaveh crashes into Linnea. Juno yanks her board up as a shield.

They all collide into the glass. It groans.

Everybody freezes.

JUNO
(whispering)
Nobody move.

A long crack spiderwebs across the window. Nobody breathes.

OSWIN
I have a key.

LINNEA
Then use it.

OSWIN
It's in my coat. Left pocket.

KAVEH
Don't touch his pocket.

LINNEA
Shut up, Kaveh.

Juno slides a hand into Oswin's left pocket. Pulls out a small brass key.

JUNO
This it?

OSWIN
Yes. Please. Careful.

Juno unlocks the chain. The briefcase pops. Papers spill.

LINNEA
Those are maps.

KAVEH
Of the mountain.

JUNO
Of the cable. Of the towers. With dates.

Linnea picks one up. Reads. Her face goes still.

LINNEA
This is my father's handwriting.

OSWIN
I'm sorry.

LINNEA
Explain.

OSWIN
Your father sold the design flaw to my company twenty years ago. I came to see if it had held.

KAVEH
It hasn't held.

OSWIN
No.

LINNEA
So this is a test.

OSWIN
A confirmation.

JUNO
You rode a broken gondola to confirm it's broken?

OSWIN
I needed to see the cable fray with my own eyes before I testify.

KAVEH
Testify to what?

OSWIN
That the company knew. That your fathers knew. That every one of us in this cabin is here because of a decision made at a conference table.

LINNEA
My father is dead.

OSWIN
I know. That's why I came.

The cabin shudders. A deep grind. Everyone looks up.

JUNO
That's the cable.

OSWIN
Yes.

LINNEA
How long?

OSWIN
Minutes.

Kaveh bolts for the door. Linnea grabs his collar. He swings. She ducks. Juno wedges her board between them.

They scuffle in the narrow aisle. The cabin tips hard to the left. All four slide to one side.

The lamp dies.

Darkness. Wind. A single metallic SNAP.

Then silence.

Then, far below, a motor kicks on. The cabin jerks. Moves. Upward.

Light floods in from the station.

They sit in a heap, panting.

JUNO
We're moving.

KAVEH
Who turned it on?

LINNEA
Backup generator. Somebody finally got to it.

She looks at Oswin. At the maps. At the three faces.

LINNEA (CONT'D)
(into radio)
Base, Strand. Four aboard. We're fine. Everybody's fine.

She tucks a map inside her jacket.
